{{Economy of Balisca}}{{Politics of Balisca}}

An '''essential industry''' ({{Lang-bl|industria esencial}}) is a legal Baliscan entity that undertakes [[W:Commerce|commercial]] activities on behalf of the [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal government]]. 

{{As of|2017}}, Balisca has the second most [[W:State-owned enterprise|state-owned enterprises]] of all countries (after China), and the second-most SOEs among large national companies. 

These essential industries accounted for over 30% of Balisca's [[W:Market capitalization|market capitalization]] in 2019 and estimates suggest that they generated about 23-28% of Balisca's [[W:Gross domestic product|GDP]] in 2017 and employ between 10% and 26% of the [[W:Workforce|workforce]]. The role of the confederal administration in IEs has varied at different periods but has decreased during the [[Bilal II Council|Bilal council]].

